# source: spec
# spec: docs/protocol/compression-lzc.md#code-packing
# provenance: PV-0060, PV-0061, PV-0062, PV-0063, PV-0065, PV-0066, PV-0067, PV-0069, PV-0080, PV-0350, PV-0310, PV-0312, PV-0384, PV-0385, PV-0386, PV-0388, PV-0395, PV-0314
# kind: decompress
# description: The single byte 0x41 as one 9-bit code.
# derivation: Header: length 1, 0x11 = LZC, 1F 9D, byte 7 = 16 | 0x80 = 0x90 (maxbits 16, block mode; PV-0310, PV-0312). The code stream starts at data byte 0 (PV-0350): code 0x041 (a literal, PV-0385) in 9 bits, least significant bit first (PV-0384, PV-0388), gives bytes 0x41 0x00 with bits 9-15 zero. Decoding stops once 1 byte is output (PV-0395).
# expect.error: none
# expect.algorithm: lzc
# expect.uncompressed_length: 1
# expect.block_mode: 1
# expect.output_length: 1
# expect.output: 41
hex:
01 00 00 00                                       # uncompressed length, u32 LE
11                                                # algorithm byte
1F 9D                                             # magic
90                                                # byte 7
41 00                                             # code 0x041 in 9 bits; 7 spare zero bits
